@startuml Authentication Flow

' ============================================================================
' Authentication Flow Diagram
' ============================================================================
' This diagram shows how Bearer Token authentication works in the API.
' All endpoints (except /health) require a valid token in the Authorization header.
'
' Token verification process (with caching):
' 1. Extract Bearer token from Authorization header
' 2. Hash the token using SHA256
' 3. Check cache for token entity (5-minute TTL)
' 4. If cache miss, query database and cache result
' 5. Validate: is_active=true, not expired
' 6. Update last_used_at only on cache miss
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2

title Bearer Token Authentication Flow (with Cache)

actor "API Client" as Client
participant "FastAPI" as API
participant "HTTPBearer" as Bearer
participant "verify_token" as Auth
participant "Cache" as Cache
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Router" as Router

== Successful Authentication (Cache Hit) ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Auth : hash_token(token)\n(SHA256)
Auth -> Cache : get(token_hash)
Cache --> Auth : ApiTokenEntity (cached)
Auth -> Auth : Validate:\n- is_active = true\n- expires_at > now()
Auth --> Bearer : Valid (ApiTokenEntity)
Bearer --> API : Authenticated
API -> Router : Process request
Router --> Client : 200 OK

== Successful Authentication (Cache Miss) ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Auth : hash_token(token)
Auth -> Cache : get(token_hash)
Cache --> Auth : NULL (cache miss)
Auth -> DB : SELECT * FROM api_tokens\nWHERE token_hash = ?
DB --> Auth : ApiToken record
Auth -> Cache : set(token_hash, entity, TTL=300s)
Auth -> DB : UPDATE last_used_at
Auth -> Auth : Validate token
Auth --> Bearer : Valid (ApiTokenEntity)
Bearer --> API : Authenticated
API -> Router : Process request
Router --> Client : 200 OK

== Token Deactivation (Cache Invalidation) ==

Client -> API : POST /tokens/{id}/deactivate
API -> Auth : verify_token(current_token)
Auth --> API : Authenticated
API -> DB : Get token by id
DB --> API : ApiToken
API -> Cache : delete(token_hash)
note right: Cache invalidation\nbefore deactivation
API -> DB : UPDATE is_active = false
API --> Client : 200 OK

== Invalid Token ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nAuthorization: Bearer wrong-token
API -> Bearer : Extract token
Bearer -> Auth : verify_token(token)
Auth -> Auth : hash_token(token)
Auth -> Cache : get(token_hash)
Cache --> Auth : NULL (cache miss)
Auth -> DB : SELECT * FROM api_tokens
DB --> Auth : NULL (not found)
Auth --> Client : 401 Unauthorized

== Missing Token ==

Client -> API : GET /experiments\nNo Authorization header
API -> Bearer : No token found
Bearer --> Client : 403 Forbidden

note right of Cache
  **Cache Strategy:**
  - TTL: 5 minutes
  - Key: token:{hash}
  - Invalidate on:
    - deactivate
    - delete
end note

note right of DB
  **api_tokens table:**
  - id, name
  - token_hash (SHA256)
  - is_active
  - created_at
  - expires_at
  - last_used_at
end note

note right of Auth
  **Performance:**
  - Cache hit: no DB query
  - last_used_at updated
    only on cache miss
end note

@enduml
